(7665472, 1249726, 251422, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> I''ve seen this before on DPC (not yours, of course... someone else''s) and still love it just as much.<br/> <br/>Well done, Susan! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thank you Lydia. Ive been doing a variation of designs with pencils for several years.  Im fairly new to DPC so I have not seen that design before.  Fun to do!</td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: I''ve seen this before on DPC (not yours, of course... someone else''s) and still love it just as much. Well done, Susan!  Thank you Lydia. Ive been doing a variation of designs with pencils for several years.  Im fairly new to DPC so I have not seen that design before.  Fun to do!', '2020-06-07 15:54:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7667237, 1249910, 30049, '<td valign="top">The silver bullet!  :-)  One thing I''m noticing as I peruse some of your images (challenge entries) is your creative use of titles.  You''re a master at it!<br/> <br/>I find this image amusing as normally most people would put the pointy end of the crayon up, which you''ve done / eluded to with the other crayons in the container.  Yet you''ve given us the opposite end.  Ha!<br/> <br/>Wondering what this looks like in B&amp;W.  Seems well suited for it with the contrast and grainy feel. You''d still know the color of the main subject as, after all, it does say ''silver'' on the side.  :-P</td>', 'The silver bullet!  :-)  One thing I''m noticing as I peruse some of your images (challenge entries) is your creative use of titles.  You''re a master at it! I find this image amusing as normally most people would put the pointy end of the crayon up, which you''ve done / eluded to with the other crayons in the container.  Yet you''ve given us the opposite end.  Ha! Wondering what this looks like in B&W.  Seems well suited for it with the contrast and grainy feel. You''d still know the color of the main subject as, after all, it does say ''silver'' on the side.  :-P', '2020-06-21 11:00:05.000000', NULL, 0),
